# arch-i686.pkgs — the 32-bit x86 half.
#
# ⛔ NO `linux` AND NO FIRMWARE PACKAGE. See build/config.sh: the `linux`
# metapackage pulls `linux-base`, which pulls 668 MB of firmware blobs for
# hardware that cannot exist in this machine. The kernel is named in config.sh
# ($KERNEL_I686) and dracut is asked for here.
#
# ⚠ THE NICS OF THIS ERA NEED NO FIRMWARE. 3c59x, Realtek 8139/8169, e1000 and
# nForce forcedeth all carry their microcode in the driver. The exception is
# Intel PRO/100 (e100), whose blob lives only inside the 500 MB
# linux-firmware-network package — if that specific card turns up, install that
# package by hand rather than putting it back here for everyone.
dracut
grub
#
# ⚠ THE VIDEO DRIVERS ARE NAMED, NOT METAPACKAGED. A Pentium 4 has whatever GPU
# it shipped with, and which one decides whether there is any acceleration at
# all. vesa is the floor and is always installed: it is what runs when none of
# the others bind. nouveau is the one that matters on the target machine — see
# docs/target-p4.md.
xf86-video-vesa
xf86-video-fbdev
xf86-video-intel
xf86-video-ati
xf86-video-nouveau
mesa-dri
